---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

// Cloud2Agent landing page. Programme rules: Drive > Cloud2Agent – Agentic AI Program > 00_Programme_Constitution.
// No fee or batch date is shown on purpose: leads go to a 1:1 call or WhatsApp.
const CALENDLY = "https://calendly.com/discover-devops";
const WHATSAPP = "918919259066";
const WA_LINK = `https://wa.me/${WHATSAPP}?text=${encodeURIComponent("Hi Rahul, I want to know more about the Cloud2Agent Agentic AI program.")}`;
const WA_FEES = `https://wa.me/${WHATSAPP}?text=${encodeURIComponent("Hi Rahul, please share the fees and next batch date for Cloud2Agent.")}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cloud2Agent – Agentic AI Program for Experienced Cloud & DevOps Professionals | Rahul Chaubey Consulting"
  description="Cloud2Agent: a 10-week live Agentic AI program for experienced Cloud, DevOps, SRE and Platform engineers. Design, build and deploy production-grade AI agents on AWS. LLMs, RAG, MCP, multi-agent systems, GitHub portfolio, interview and career support."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">


<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero first">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Live program · 10 weekends · For experienced Cloud &amp; DevOps professionals</p>
    <h1><span class="brand">Cloud2Agent</span><br>Agentic AI Engineering &amp; Architecture</h1>
    <p class="sub">Design, build and deploy production-grade Agentic AI systems on cloud, using the Cloud and DevOps experience you already have.</p>
    <p class="lead">Think like an AI Solution Architect. Build like an AI Engineer. Deploy like a Cloud/DevOps Engineer. You don't restart your career. You add the AI layer on top of it.</p>
    <div class="btns">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"/></svg>
        Book a free 1:1 call with Rahul</a>
      <a class="btn btn-wa" href={WA_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2a10 10 0 0 0-8.6 15.1L2 22l5-1.3A10 10 0 1 0 12 2zm0 18.2c-1.5 0-3-.4-4.2-1.2l-.3-.2-3 .8.8-2.9-.2-.3A8.2 8.2 0 1 1 12 20.2zm4.5-6.1c-.2-.1-1.5-.7-1.7-.8-.2-.1-.4-.1-.6.1l-.8 1c-.1.2-.3.2-.5.1a6.7 6.7 0 0 1-3.3-2.9c-.2-.4.2-.4.7-1.3.1-.2 0-.3 0-.4l-.8-1.8c-.2-.5-.4-.4-.6-.4h-.5a1 1 0 0 0-.7.3 3 3 0 0 0-.9 2.2 5.1 5.1 0 0 0 1.1 2.7 11.7 11.7 0 0 0 4.5 4c1.7.7 2.3.8 3.2.6.5-.1 1.5-.6 1.7-1.2.2-.6.2-1.1.2-1.2-.1-.1-.2-.2-.5-.3z"/></svg>
        WhatsApp Rahul</a>
    </div>
    <div class="facts">
      <div><small>Duration</small><strong>10 weekends</strong></div>
      <div><small>Live hours</small><strong>80 hours</strong></div>
      <div><small>Schedule</small><strong>Sat 4h + Sun 4h</strong></div>
      <div><small>Hands-on cloud</small><strong>AWS + Azure mapping</strong></div>
      <div><small>You build</small><strong>9 projects + capstone</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHO -->
<section id="who">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Is this for you?</p>
    <h2>Built only for experienced professionals</h2>
    <p class="lead">Ideally 5–20 years in IT, with real exposure to Cloud, DevOps, infrastructure, software or architecture.</p>
    <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:28px">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>This program is for you if you are a</h3>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>DevOps Engineer or Senior Cloud Engineer (AWS/Azure)</li>
          <li>SRE or Platform Engineer</li>
          <li>Cloud, Solution or Technical Architect</li>
          <li>Engineering Manager or Technical Lead</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>This program is not for you if you are</h3>
        <ul class="cross">
          <li>A fresher or student without industry experience</li>
          <li>Expecting Cloud or Linux fundamentals from scratch</li>
          <li>Looking for basic Python training</li>
          <li>Expecting a placement guarantee</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">This program does not teach Cloud fundamentals, Linux fundamentals or programming from scratch. Not sure if you fit? <a href={CALENDLY} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>Book a free 1:1 call</b></a> and Rahul will tell you honestly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OUTCOME -->
<section id="outcome">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The outcome</p>
    <h2>After 10 weekends, you will be able to</h2>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:28px">
      <div class="card"><h3>Understand</h3><p>How LLMs, Transformers, RAG, AI agents, MCP and multi-agent systems really work, and when not to use them.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Design</h3><p>Enterprise-grade Agentic AI architectures with security, identity, scalability, reliability and observability built in.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Build &amp; deploy</h3><p>Working AI applications in Python, deployed on AWS with containers, IaC and CI/CD, and mapped to Azure.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:24px">The goal is not another chatbot or proof of concept. It is the ability to design and deliver production-grade AI systems inside a real enterprise.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- METHOD -->
<section id="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How you learn</p>
    <h2>Every topic follows the same six steps</h2>
    <p class="lead">Not mathematics-heavy. Engineering and architecture first. You learn to understand, review and modify AI-generated code using ChatGPT, Claude Code and OpenAI Codex.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div><b>Context</b><span>Why does it exist?</span></div>
      <div><b>Concept</b><span>How does it work?</span></div>
      <div><b>Architecture</b><span>How do parts connect?</span></div>
      <div><b>Lab</b><span>Build it yourself</span></div>
      <div><b>Production</b><span>Run it in an enterprise</span></div>
      <div><b>Interview</b><span>Explain and defend it</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CURRICULUM -->
<section id="curriculum">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Curriculum</p>
    <h2>10 weekends, week by week</h2>
    <p class="lead">Every weekend has a clear goal, a project and a new addition to your GitHub. Tap a week to see all topics.</p>
    <button class="expand-all" type="button" id="toggleAll">Expand all weeks</button>
    <div class="weeks">

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 1</span><span class="wt">AI, LLMs and Transformer Architecture<span class="wp">How AI evolved, how LLMs work, and what happens inside a Transformer.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – AI and LLM foundations</h4><ul>
              <li>Traditional programming vs AI; Machine Learning types</li>
              <li>Deep learning, neural networks, training vs inference</li>
              <li>From ML to Generative AI; rule-based vs LLMs vs agents</li>
              <li>What an LLM is; next-token prediction</li>
              <li>Tokens, tokenization, context windows, parameters</li>
              <li>Pre-training, fine-tuning, inference; hallucinations</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Transformer architecture</h4><ul>
              <li>Why Transformers; RNN and LSTM limits</li>
              <li>Embeddings and positional encoding</li>
              <li>Self-attention: Query, Key, Value, Softmax</li>
              <li>Causal masking and multi-head attention</li>
              <li>Feed-forward, residuals, layer normalization</li>
              <li>Encoder vs decoder; why GPT is decoder-only</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>A documented Transformer explanation with diagrams, from input text to generated output.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>AI and LLM fundamentals repo with diagrams and notes.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 2</span><span class="wt">Python Foundations and AI-Assisted Coding<span class="wp">Enough Python to read, review, modify and run AI-generated applications.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – Python for AI engineering</h4><ul>
              <li>Project setup, virtual environments, dependencies</li>
              <li>Data types, lists, dictionaries, loops, functions</li>
              <li>Modules, packages, classes (only what you need)</li>
              <li>Exceptions, JSON, files, HTTP requests, async basics</li>
              <li>Config, environment variables, project structure</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – AI-assisted engineering</h4><ul>
              <li>ChatGPT, Claude Code and OpenAI Codex for Python</li>
              <li>Writing clear instructions for coding agents</li>
              <li>Reviewing, debugging and testing generated code</li>
              <li>Git and GitHub workflow</li>
              <li>Handling credentials and secrets safely</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>A FastAPI service with Pydantic models, config, structured logging, health check, error handling and tests.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>Your first working Python application with README and setup steps.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 3</span><span class="wt">LLM Engineering and AI Application Architecture<span class="wp">Integrate foundation models into real applications using Amazon Bedrock.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – Working with LLMs</h4><ul>
              <li>Foundation models, providers and model APIs</li>
              <li>Amazon Bedrock as the main platform</li>
              <li>System, user and assistant messages; prompt engineering</li>
              <li>Temperature, structured JSON output, streaming</li>
              <li>Tokens, latency, cost, limits, retries</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Building LLM applications</h4><ul>
              <li>LLM application architecture and prompt templates</li>
              <li>Conversation history and app-level memory</li>
              <li>External API integration; model selection trade-offs</li>
              <li>Config, secrets, logging and error handling</li>
              <li>Separating business logic from model calls</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>A Python AI Assistant with structured responses, conversation context and operational logging.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>LLM application + architecture doc. Azure mapping: Azure OpenAI, AI Foundry.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 4</span><span class="wt">Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)<span class="wp">Give AI grounded answers from private company knowledge.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – RAG fundamentals</h4><ul>
              <li>Why LLMs need external knowledge</li>
              <li>RAG architecture and data flow</li>
              <li>Ingestion, parsing and chunking strategies</li>
              <li>Metadata, embeddings, vector databases</li>
              <li>Similarity search and context building</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Advanced RAG engineering</h4><ul>
              <li>Top-K, metadata filtering, hybrid search, reranking</li>
              <li>Query transformation and decomposition</li>
              <li>Grounded answers with citations</li>
              <li>RAG failure modes and evaluation</li>
              <li>Agentic RAG; RAG on AWS services</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>An Enterprise Knowledge Base Assistant that answers from company documents with source references.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>RAG pipeline, ingestion, diagram, evaluation. Azure mapping: Azure AI Search.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 5</span><span class="wt">Agentic AI and Agents from Scratch<span class="wp">Understand what makes an app agentic, then build the agent loop yourself.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – Agentic AI fundamentals</h4><ul>
              <li>LLM vs chatbot vs assistant vs agent</li>
              <li>Workflows vs autonomous agents</li>
              <li>Planning, task decomposition, execution loop</li>
              <li>Tool calling, function calling, tool schemas</li>
              <li>Agent memory; human-in-the-loop; when not to use agents</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Building agents in Python</h4><ul>
              <li>Defining, validating and executing tools</li>
              <li>Building the agent loop</li>
              <li>Retries, limits and stopping conditions</li>
              <li>Permission boundaries and human approval</li>
              <li>Agentic RAG patterns</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>A Cloud Operations Assistant that reads runbooks, calls approved read-only tools and recommends the next action.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>Tool-using agent with documented execution flow.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 6</span><span class="wt">Model Context Protocol (MCP) and Enterprise Integration<span class="wp">Connect agents securely to enterprise tools, systems and data.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – MCP architecture</h4><ul>
              <li>The enterprise integration problem</li>
              <li>MCP Host, Client and Server</li>
              <li>Tools, Resources and Prompts</li>
              <li>Tool discovery, invocation and lifecycle</li>
              <li>MCP vs traditional API integration</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Building MCP integrations</h4><ul>
              <li>Build an MCP server in Python</li>
              <li>Connect a client and an agent</li>
              <li>Access control, auth and security</li>
              <li>Containerize and deploy MCP services</li>
              <li>Enterprise integration patterns</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>An MCP server exposing approved tools and knowledge, connected to your Week 5 agent.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>MCP server, client integration, diagram and setup docs.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 7</span><span class="wt">Multi-Agent Systems and Agent Frameworks<span class="wp">Make specialised agents work together, and choose the right framework.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – Multi-agent architecture</h4><ul>
              <li>Single vs multi-agent; specialised roles</li>
              <li>Orchestrator and worker pattern</li>
              <li>Sequential, parallel and hierarchical execution</li>
              <li>Shared state, delegation, failure recovery</li>
              <li>Human-in-the-loop orchestration</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Agent frameworks</h4><ul>
              <li>LangChain components</li>
              <li>LangGraph: nodes, edges, state, checkpoints, approvals</li>
              <li>CrewAI: agents, tasks, crews</li>
              <li>LangChain vs LangGraph vs CrewAI</li>
              <li>Framework vs building from scratch</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>A multi-agent Cloud Operations or research workflow with an orchestrator and shared context.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>Multi-agent code, workflow diagram and framework comparison.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 8</span><span class="wt">Enterprise Architecture and Deployment on AWS<span class="wp">Move from local prototype to production-oriented cloud architecture.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – Enterprise architecture design</h4><ul>
              <li>Prototype vs production architecture</li>
              <li>Sync vs async; event-driven AI workflows</li>
              <li>Queues and long-running agent workflows</li>
              <li>Stateful vs stateless; scaling AI apps</li>
              <li>Serverless vs containers; networking; trade-offs</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – AWS implementation</h4><ul>
              <li>Bedrock, S3, Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, SQS</li>
              <li>Docker, ECR, ECS / EKS</li>
              <li>IAM permissions and Secrets Manager</li>
              <li>Infrastructure as Code and CI/CD</li>
              <li>Choosing the right AWS pattern for AI workloads</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>Your AI application deployed on AWS in a documented, controlled environment.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>Deployment code, IaC, diagram, docs. Azure mapping: Functions, Container Apps, AKS.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 9</span><span class="wt">Security, Evaluation, Monitoring and LLMOps<span class="wp">Secure, test, observe and operate AI systems like production software.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – AI security and governance</h4><ul>
              <li>Prompt injection (direct and indirect)</li>
              <li>Data leakage and sensitive data exposure</li>
              <li>Tool security, least privilege, IAM boundaries</li>
              <li>Guardrails, approvals, audit logging</li>
              <li>Responsible AI; multi-agent security</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Evaluation, monitoring, LLMOps</h4><ul>
              <li>LLM, RAG and agent evaluation</li>
              <li>Evaluation datasets and regression testing</li>
              <li>Tracing, logs, metrics; token and latency monitoring</li>
              <li>Cost optimisation and reliability</li>
              <li>CI/CD for AI; CloudWatch monitoring</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>A hardened, evaluated and monitored version of your AI application.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>Security checklist, eval suite, monitoring docs. Azure mapping: Entra ID, Azure Monitor.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="week">
        <summary><span class="wk">Week 10</span><span class="wt">Capstone and Career Readiness<span class="wp">Present your enterprise platform, then prepare your portfolio, LinkedIn, resume and interviews.</span></span><span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="wbody">
          <div class="days">
            <div><h4>Saturday – Capstone demo</h4><ul>
              <li>Enterprise Cloud Operations Agentic AI Platform</li>
              <li>Architecture walkthrough and live demo</li>
              <li>Security and permission model</li>
              <li>Evaluation results and design decisions</li></ul></div>
            <div><h4>Sunday – Career readiness</h4><ul>
              <li>GitHub portfolio review</li>
              <li>LinkedIn positioning and project posts</li>
              <li>Resume tailored to AI job descriptions</li>
              <li>Interview and mock-interview preparation</li>
              <li>Job search and application strategy</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <div class="out"><div><b>You build</b>The final capstone, a documented GitHub portfolio and a career-readiness plan.</div><div><b>Your GitHub</b>Capstone repo with architecture, README, deployment and evaluation.</div></div>
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CAPSTONE -->
<section id="capstone">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your capstone</p>
      <h2>Enterprise Cloud Operations Agentic AI Platform</h2>
      <p>Cloud and DevOps teams fight incidents, search runbooks and dig through monitoring data every day. You build an AI platform that helps engineers investigate, gather evidence and recommend fixes, with a human approving anything sensitive. It is a project you can explain in any interview, because it solves your own daily problem.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Natural-language operational questions</li>
        <li>RAG over runbooks and architecture docs</li>
        <li>Planning and specialised agents</li>
        <li>Approved tools connected through MCP</li>
        <li>Read-only evidence gathering and verification</li>
        <li>Human approval before sensitive actions</li>
        <li>Audit history and investigation reports</li>
        <li>Deployed on AWS with IAM, evaluation and observability</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT YOU GET -->
<section id="get" class="gets">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What you get</p>
    <h2>More than 80 hours of classes</h2>
    <p class="lead">This is a technical and career transformation program. Here is everything included.</p>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:28px">
      <div class="card"><p class="num">01</p><h3>Enterprise AI skills</h3><p>LLMs, RAG, agents, MCP, multi-agent systems, security and AWS deployment, with Azure equivalents.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="num">02</p><h3>Your GitHub portfolio</h3><p>Built step by step, one project every week, with READMEs, architecture diagrams and design decisions.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="num">03</p><h3>Interview questions for every topic</h3><p>Concept, direct, architecture, scenario and troubleshooting questions, and how to answer them.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="num">04</p><h3>LinkedIn profile</h3><p>Headline, About section, project showcases and posts that reflect what you built.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="num">05</p><h3>Resume and job applications</h3><p>A project-based resume, help finding matching roles, CV tailored to each job, and help applying.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="num">06</p><h3>Mock interviews and recordings</h3><p>Mock interviews with Rahul, honest feedback, and recordings of every live session.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">We give real job-search and application support. We do not promise employment or guaranteed placement.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GITHUB -->
<section id="github">
  <div class="wrap grid2" style="align-items:center">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Proof of skill</p>
      <h2>Your GitHub after 10 weeks</h2>
      <p class="lead">Recruiters and hiring managers don't just read your resume. They open your GitHub. By the last weekend, yours shows real, documented, working AI systems.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="repo">
      <div><span class="dir">01-ai-llm-foundations/</span> <span class="c"># Transformer diagrams</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">02-python-fastapi-service/</span> <span class="c"># first service</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">03-llm-assistant-bedrock/</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">04-enterprise-rag-assistant/</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">05-cloudops-agent/</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">06-mcp-server/</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">07-multi-agent-workflow/</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">08-aws-deployment/</span> <span class="c"># IaC + CI/CD</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">09-security-eval-llmops/</span></div>
      <div><span class="dir">capstone-cloudops-agentic-platform/</span> <span class="c"># ★</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INSTRUCTOR -->
<section id="instructor">
  <div class="wrap inst">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Your instructor</p>
      <h2>Rahul Chaubey</h2>
      <p class="lead">Director, Cloud and AI Engineering. Two decades in IT, from Solaris/Unix sysadmin to AWS, DevOps lead, Technical Account Manager and cloud architect. He teaches what he builds and runs every day.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="creds">
      <li>Two decades of enterprise IT across AWS, Azure and Oracle environments</li>
      <li>Built a cloud and AI engineering practice from zero to about forty engineers</li>
      <li>M.Tech in Data Science &amp; Machine Learning, BITS Pilani</li>
      <li>Executive General Management Programme, IIM Bangalore</li>
      <li>Professional Certificate in Agentic AI, IIT Madras</li>
      <li>Five years of running live batches for working professionals</li>
      <li>YouTube: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@BuildAutomateArchitect" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Build Automate Architect</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/chaubeyrahul/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FEES -->
<section id="fees">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Fees and next batch</p>
    <h2>Talk to Rahul first</h2>
    <p class="lead">Seats are limited so every student gets project reviews and mock interviews. Fees, payment options and the next batch date are shared on a free 1:1 call, where Rahul also checks that the program fits your experience and goals.</p>
    <div class="btns">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a free 1:1 call with Rahul</a>
      <a class="btn btn-wa" href={WA_FEES} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ask on WhatsApp: +91-8919259066</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq" class="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <details><summary>Do I need to know Python?</summary><p>Basic familiarity helps, but it is not required. Week 2 is a full weekend on the Python you need, plus using AI coding assistants. Recorded Python lessons are also provided for revision. You are not trained as a Python developer; you learn to understand, review and modify AI-generated code.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need a maths or data-science background?</summary><p>No. We explain the intuition behind the maths. Advanced derivations are optional reading. The focus is engineering and architecture.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is Azure covered?</summary><p>All hands-on labs and deployments use AWS. For every major design, we map the equivalent Azure services and architecture, so you can explain both in interviews.</p></details>
    <details><summary>I am a fresher. Can I join?</summary><p>No. Cloud2Agent is only for experienced professionals with real Cloud, DevOps, SRE, software or architecture exposure. It does not teach Cloud, Linux or programming from scratch.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if I miss a live session?</summary><p>Every live session is recorded, so you can watch it and catch up before the next weekend.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will I get a job after this program?</summary><p>We help you build your GitHub, LinkedIn and resume, find matching roles, tailor your CV and apply, and we run mock interviews. We do not promise or guarantee placement.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What are the fees and when does the next batch start?</summary><p>Book a free 1:1 call with Rahul or send a WhatsApp message to +91-8919259066. Fees, payment options and dates are shared there.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

